Description: Network identity of Citronics phones, unique per device
 Derives from the eMMC serial the address of the phone's USB network link
 (usb0), the address its DHCP server hands the computer, and the link's
 MAC: a /30 in 10.250.0.0/16, so that phones connected to the same computer
 never clash. Configures isc-dhcp-server or dnsmasq, whichever serves the
 link. Gives a Wi-Fi interface that has no MAC (the FP3's) a stable one,
 02:00:<eMMC serial>.

